  "name": "Example: Solving a \"Less Than or Equal To\" Inequality Given the Graph of the Corresponding Parabola",
  "problem": "Given the graph below, solve the inequality $-x^2+2x+3 \\leq 0.$    \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/93fa79fb8411a6bdf16b3eb9c1aab489377a9b0d039b0be4b884f8cdc47bf683.png)",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-x^2+2x+3 \\leq 0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*less than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny =-x^2+2x+3\n$$\n\nis *below* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/6b11e0ab1c3cd92003d3b5330b4eab64e192efbe1953cfbc560b717ccc0e3c57.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x \\leq -1$ or $x \\geq 3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
